---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Icon from '../components/icons/Icon.astro';

const lastUpdated = 'April 30, 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How Chancey collects, uses, and protects your account data, picks, ticket scans, preferences, logs, and support messages."
  breadcrumbs={[
    { name: 'Home', href: '/' },
    { name: 'Privacy Policy', href: '/privacy/' },
  ]}
>
  <section class="container">
    <div class="article">
      <header>
        <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
        <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="muted">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>
        <div class="notice">
          <span class="notice-icon" aria-hidden="true"><Icon name="lightning" size={22} /></span>
          <div>
            <strong>Working draft</strong>
            This policy is in final legal review for launch. Big changes will show up in the app
            and at the top of this page.
          </div>
        </div>
      </header>

      <section>
        <h2>The short version</h2>
        <p>
          Chancey is for adults 18+ who want to pick and track lottery tickets. To do that, we
          store your account info, the picks and tickets you save, your settings, and the logs we
          need to run the app. We do not sell your data. We do not show ads inside the app. We do
          not use ticket photos for advertising.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Information we collect</h2>
        <h3>Account information</h3>
        <p>
          When you sign up, we store an email (or an ID from a sign-in service you choose), an
          attestation that you are 18 or older, and any settings you pick. We may store hashed
          tokens to keep you signed in.
        </p>
        <h3>Picks, ticket scans, and saved data</h3>
        <p>
          When you pick numbers or scan a ticket, we save the numbers, the game, the draw date,
          and any notes you add. Ticket photos are processed to read the numbers and details. If
          your device cannot read a number on its own, we may use a cloud step to help. We never
          use ticket photos for advertising or sell them to third parties.
        </p>
        <h3>Preferences and app state</h3>
        <p>
          We store your settings — favorites, saved sets, reminder choices — so the app works the
          same way across your devices.
        </p>
        <h3>Operational logs</h3>
        <p>
          We collect the logs we need to run, debug, and protect the service: timestamps, IP
          addresses, device and browser type, error reports, and request data. We keep these for a
          limited time. They are used for operations and security, not for ads.
        </p>
        <h3>Support messages</h3>
        <p>
          When you write to support, we keep the message and any attachments so we can reply,
          follow up, and improve the product. Don't send government IDs, payment cards, or
          passwords.
        </p>
        <h3>Analytics on this marketing site</h3>
        <p>
          The marketing site at chancey.io uses Google Analytics 4 (GA4) to count visits, see
          which pages people read, and measure clicks on the call-to-action buttons. We have GA4
          set up with privacy-respecting defaults: IP addresses are anonymized, advertising
          features are off, and no cross-site advertising signals are sent. GA4 sets a first-party
          <code>_ga</code> cookie. The Chancey web app at app.chancey.io does not load advertising
          trackers.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>How we use information</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>To run the core service: picks, scanning, history, draw matching, and sync.</li>
          <li>To sign you in and keep accounts safe.</li>
          <li>To debug issues and keep the service reliable and secure.</li>
          <li>To reply to your support and privacy requests.</li>
          <li>To meet the law where it applies.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          We do not use your information to sell ads, build ad profiles, or share with data
          brokers. We only use ticket photos to read the numbers and draw details.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Sharing</h2>
        <p>We share information only with:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Service providers</strong> who run our infrastructure (hosting, sign-in, error
            tracking, optional ticket-recognition help, email delivery, web analytics). These
            providers are bound by contract to protect data and use it only for what we ask.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Legal recipients</strong> when the law, a valid legal process, or the safety
            of users requires it.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Successors</strong> if Chancey is sold or merged. We will require continued
            protection of your data and tell you about meaningful changes.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Your choices</h2>
        <p>
          You can ask for access to your data, a correction, a deletion, or an export. Send a
          message through our <a href="/contact/">contact form</a> and pick the "Privacy or data
          request" topic. Use the email tied to your account. We reply within the windows the law
          requires (usually 30 days).
        </p>
        <h3>Cookies and similar tools</h3>
        <p>
          The marketing site uses essential cookies and a privacy-respecting Google Analytics
          cookie (see above). The Chancey web app uses essential cookies and similar storage for
          sign-in and settings. We do not run cross-site advertising trackers. To opt out of GA4,
          you can use your browser's tracking-prevention setting, install the
          <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" rel="noopener">Google Analytics
            opt-out add-on</a>, or block analytics cookies in your browser.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Children</h2>
        <p>
          Chancey is not for anyone under 18, or under the local age of majority, whichever is
          greater. We do not knowingly collect data from children. If you think a child gave us
          data, send a message through the <a href="/contact/">contact form</a> and we will delete
          it.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Security</h2>
        <p>
          We use reasonable safeguards — administrative, technical, and physical — to protect your
          data. No system is perfect. If we learn of an incident that affects your data, we will
          tell you and the right regulators in line with the law.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Changes</h2>
        <p>
          We will update this policy as the product changes. Big changes will show up in the app
          and at the top of this page, with a new "last updated" date.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
          For privacy questions or to use the rights above, send a message through the <a
            href="/contact/">contact form</a> and pick the "Privacy or data request" topic.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
